  "table_html": "\n\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <h2>Worked example - feature #3</h2>\n  <p>The feature that moved the most among the reliable ones, at $\\mathbf u = (328,\\ 867)$\n    in frame $t$. The window is 21 &times; 21 pixels and the pyramid has\n    4 levels. Gradients $I_x, I_y$ come from the Scharr filter divided by 32, in grey levels per pixel.</p>\n\n  <h3>1. Structure tensor at level 0</h3>\n  <div class=\"theory-block\">\n    $$ G = \\sum_W \\begin{bmatrix} I_x^2 & I_xI_y \\\\ I_xI_y & I_y^2 \\end{bmatrix}\n         = \\begin{bmatrix} 282297.6 & -30111.9 \\\\ -30111.9 & 344931.3 \\end{bmatrix},\n       \\qquad \\lambda_1 = 357059.5,\\ \\ \\lambda_2 = 270169.3 $$\n  </div>\n  <p>Both eigenvalues are large (per window pixel $\\lambda_2 / 441 = 612.6$,\n    and the threshold is 0.01). The ratio is $\\lambda_1/\\lambda_2 = 1.32$, so this is a\n    corner and not an edge, and $G$ is safely invertible.</p>\n\n  <h3>2. Iterations at level 0</h3>\n  <p>The coarser pyramid levels hand down the initial guess\n    $\\mathbf g^0 = (5.144,\\ 0.569)$. Each row solves\n    $G\\boldsymbol\\delta = \\mathbf b_k$ with $\\mathbf b_k = \\sum_W \\big(I(\\mathbf x) - J(\\mathbf x + \\mathbf d_k)\\big)\\,[I_x, I_y]^{\\mathsf T}$,\n    where $J$ is sampled with bilinear interpolation.</p>\n  <table class=\"result-table\">\n    <tr><th>k</th><th>$\\mathbf d_k$ (x, y)</th><th>$\\mathbf b_k$</th><th>$\\boldsymbol\\delta = G^{-1}\\mathbf b_k$</th><th>$|\\boldsymbol\\delta|$</th><th>RMS $I - J$</th></tr>\n    \n    <tr><td>0</td>\n      <td>(5.1439, 0.5688)</td>\n      <td>(32596.9, 31771.1)</td>\n      <td>(+0.1265, +0.1031)</td>\n      <td>0.1632</td>\n      <td>10.26</td></tr>\n    \n    <tr><td>1</td>\n      <td>(5.2703, 0.6719)</td>\n      <td>(-3225.4, -4904.4)</td>\n      <td>(-0.0131, -0.0154)</td>\n      <td>0.0202</td>\n      <td>9.53</td></tr>\n    \n    <tr><td>2</td>\n      <td>(5.2573, 0.6566)</td>\n      <td>(370.5, 715.9)</td>\n      <td>(+0.0015, +0.0022)</td>\n      <td>0.0027</td>\n      <td>9.51</td></tr>\n    \n  </table>\n  <p class=\"muted\">The iteration stops when $|\\boldsymbol\\delta| < 0.01$ px. This one converged in 3 step(s).</p>\n\n  <h3>3. Prediction vs. actual</h3>\n  <div class=\"theory-block\">\n    $$ \\mathbf u' = \\mathbf u + \\mathbf d = (328,\\ 867) + (5.259,\\ 0.659)\n       = (333.259,\\ 867.659) $$\n    $$ \\text{actual (NCC peak)} = (333.242,\\ 867.678), \\qquad\n       \\lVert \\mathbf u' - \\mathbf u'_{\\text{actual}} \\rVert = 0.026\\ \\text{px} $$\n    $$ \\text{OpenCV LK: } \\mathbf d = (5.259,\\ 0.659), \\qquad\n       \\text{difference from ours} = 0.0000\\ \\text{px} $$\n  </div>\n  <p>Brightness constancy check: the mean $|I(\\mathbf x) - J(\\mathbf x + \\mathbf d)|$ over the window drops from\n    59.08 grey levels at $\\mathbf d = \\mathbf 0$ to 6.91 at the tracked $\\mathbf d$.</p>\n\n  <h3>4. Bilinear interpolation at the tracked position</h3>\n  <p>The centre of the window lands at $(x, y) = (333.2588,\\ 867.6588)$ in frame $t+1$, so\n    $x_0 = 333$, $y_0 = 867$, $a = 0.2588$, $b = 0.6588$. The four neighbours are:</p>\n  <div class=\"theory-block\">\n    $$ \\begin{bmatrix} f_{00} & f_{10} \\\\ f_{01} & f_{11} \\end{bmatrix}\n       = \\begin{bmatrix} 240 & 235 \\\\ 239 & 241 \\end{bmatrix} $$\n    $$ f(x, y_0) = (1-a)f_{00} + a f_{10} = 0.7412\\cdot240 + 0.2588\\cdot235 = 238.7058 $$\n    $$ f(x, y_0{+}1) = (1-a)f_{01} + a f_{11} = 0.7412\\cdot239 + 0.2588\\cdot241 = 239.5177 $$\n    $$ f(x, y) = (1-b)\\,238.7058 + b\\,239.5177 = 239.2407 $$\n  </div>\n  <p>Equivalently, the weights $(1-a)(1-b), a(1-b), (1-a)b, ab$ are\n    0.2529, 0.0883, 0.4883, 0.1705\n    (sum 1.0000). OpenCV's <code>getRectSubPix</code> at the same point gives\n    239.2407 (difference 2.0e-05, which is float32 rounding).\n    For comparison, the pixel at $\\mathbf u$ in frame $t$ is 237: the interpolated\n    value in frame $t+1$ is close to it, as brightness constancy says it should be.</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <h2>Every tracked feature</h2>\n  <p class=\"muted\">All positions in pixels. \"Actual\" is the NCC template-match location in frame t+1. Grey rows\n    have a weak match (NCC &le; 0.9, e.g. on a motion boundary or in repeated texture) and are left out of the statistics.</p>\n  <div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\n  <table class=\"result-table\">\n    <tr><th>#</th><th>u (frame t)</th><th>d (our LK)</th><th>predicted u + d</th><th>actual</th><th>error</th>\n      <th>d (OpenCV)</th><th>NCC</th><th>$\\lambda_2$/px</th><th>residual</th></tr>\n    \n    <tr style=\"opacity:.5\">\n      <td>1</td><td>(270, 21)</td>\n      <td>(0.325, -1.525)</td>\n      <td>(270.33, 19.47)</td>\n      <td>(270.07, 19.68)</td>\n      <td>0.324</td>\n      <td>(0.325, -1.525)</td>\n      <td>0.757</td>\n      <td>299.3</td>\n      <td>35.7 &rarr; 16.5</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr style=\"opacity:.5\">\n      <td>2</td><td>(491, 42)</td>\n      <td>(1.544, -1.797)</td>\n      <td>(492.54, 40.20)</td>\n      <td>(492.62, 39.96)</td>\n      <td>0.251</td>\n      <td>(1.544, -1.797)</td>\n      <td>0.827</td>\n      <td>248.4</td>\n      <td>43.7 &rarr; 12.4</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr >\n      <td>3</td><td>(328, 867)</td>\n      <td>(5.259, 0.659)</td>\n      <td>(333.26, 867.66)</td>\n      <td>(333.24, 867.68)</td>\n      <td>0.026</td>\n      <td>(5.259, 0.659)</td>\n      <td>0.958</td>\n      <td>612.6</td>\n      <td>59.1 &rarr; 6.9</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr >\n      <td>4</td><td>(351, 24)</td>\n      <td>(0.930, -2.088)</td>\n      <td>(351.93, 21.91)</td>\n      <td>(351.99, 21.96)</td>\n      <td>0.072</td>\n      <td>(0.930, -2.088)</td>\n      <td>0.922</td>\n      <td>251.8</td>\n      <td>38.2 &rarr; 10.6</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr style=\"opacity:.5\">\n      <td>5</td><td>(290, 229)</td>\n      <td>(0.435, -1.298)</td>\n      <td>(290.43, 227.70)</td>\n      <td>(290.12, 227.93)</td>\n      <td>0.387</td>\n      <td>(0.435, -1.298)</td